o-CEO Ted Sarandos has said the streamer needs new avenues for growth and to improve execution aro...\n\n3 days ago - CNBC\n\n### Ads Offer Netflix Flexibility: Phillips Securities' Wang\n\nNetflix is struggling to attract new subscribers and boost engagement as it tries to find its next big film or TV hit. Helena Wang, Phillips Securities research analyst, discusses how the streaming gi...\n\n3 days ago - Bloomberg Technology\n\n### Netflix Jitters: Valid Concerns Or Market Overreaction? – “One Breakout Hit Could Shift Sentiment”\n\nNetflix shares skidded 4% Wednesday after mixed-to-uninspiring quarterly earnings as Wall Streeters cut price targets on the stock. Analysts want proof of more muscular viewer engagement.\n\n### Netflix's stock just collapsed to a 2-year low: Is the streaming giant's ad business in trouble?\n\nShares in Netflix Inc. (Nasdaq: NFLX) have fallen to a more than a two-year low after the streaming giant posted its Q3 2026 results yesterday.\n\n3 days ago - Fast Company\n\n### Is Netflix losing one of its longest-standing edge?\n\nNetflix (NFLX) faces a question that one disappointing earnings outlook cannot fully explain: does Hollywood's biggest entertainment budget still buy a durable competitive advantage? NFLX shares are d...\n\n### Netflix Stock Drops After a Disappointing Outlook\n\nNetflix shares are tumbling after a weaker-than-expected forecast.\n\n### NFLX Taps 2-Year Low After Earnings: What Has Investors Dialing Down Bullishness\n\nNetflix (NFLX) posted a double miss on earnings, a report that has investors shaping their outlook on the streaming giant as companies like Skydance (SKYD) pose a larger threat to the company's bottom...\n\n### Netflix stock falls as analysts question growth despite earnings beat\n\nNetflix shares NFLX fell in trading on Wednesday after its third-quarter earnings exceeded expectations, but a weaker revenue forecast and concerns about slowing engagement raised questions about its ...\n\n### Netflix Earnings Beat Expectations, but Growth Expectations Come Up Short\n\nNetflix reported earnings for the third quarter that exceeded Wall Street expectations, but forecast a fourth consecutive quarter of slowing sales growth, a projection that may amplify concerns about ...\n\n3 days ago - Bloomberg Technology","title":"Netflix (NFLX) Stock Price & Overview","url":"https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/nflx/"},{"author":null,"id":"https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/nflx/statistics/","image":"https://stockanalysis.com/stockanalysis-1200x630.png","text":"Netflix (NFLX) Statistics & Valuation\n\n65.85 -1.20 (-1.79%) At close: Oct 23, 2026, 4:00 PM EDT\n\n65.75 -0.10 (-0.15%) After-hours: Oct 23, 2026, 7:59 PM EDT\n\n## Total Valuation\n\nNetflix has a market cap or net worth of $270.40 billion. The enterprise value is $279.71 billion.\n\n| Market Cap | 270.40B |\n| --- | --- |\n| Enterprise Value | 279.71B |\n\n## Important Dates\n\nThe last earnings date was Tuesday, October 20, 2026, after market close.\n\n| Earnings Date | Oct 20, 2026 |\n| --- | --- |\n| Ex-Dividend Date | n/a |\n\n## Share Statistics\n\nNetflix has 4.11 billion shares outstanding. The number of shares has decreased by -2.10% in one year.\n\n| Current Share Class | 4.11B |\n| --- | --- |\n| Shares Outstanding | 4.11B |\n| Shares Change (YoY) | -2.10% |\n| Shares Change (QoQ) | -1.55% |\n| Owned by Insiders (%) | 0.59% |\n| Owned by Institutions (%) | 84.37% |\n| Float | 4.08B |\n\n## Valuation Ratios\n\nThe trailing PE ratio is 19.06 and the forward PE ratio is 18.34. Netflix's PEG ratio is 0.88.\n\n| PE Ratio | 19.06 |\n| --- | --- |\n| Forward PE | 18.34 |\n| PS Ratio | 5.44 |\n| Forward PS | 4.90 |\n| PB Ratio | 9.23 |\n| P/TBV Ratio | 16.12 |\n| P/FCF Ratio | 23.77 |\n| P/OCF Ratio | 21.97 |\n| PEG Ratio | 0.88 |\n\n## Enterprise Valuation\n\nThe stock's EV/EBITDA ratio is 17.53, with an EV/FCF ratio of 24.59.\n\n| EV / Earnings | 18.94 |\n| --- | --- |\n| EV / Sales | 5.62 |\n| EV / EBITDA | 17.53 |\n| EV /