ps and operates proprietary technology applications in the United States, Canada, Latin America, Europe, the Middle East, Africa, and the Asia Pacific. The company operates through three segments: Mobility, Delivery, and Freight. The Mobility segment connects consumers with a range of transportation modalities, such as ridesharing, carsharing, micromobility, rentals, public transit, taxis, and other modalities; and offers riders in a variety of vehicle types, as well as financial partnerships products and advertisi... [Read more]\n\nIndustry Software - Application Sector Technology IPO Date May 10, 2019 Employees 36,600 Stock Exchange NYSE Ticker Symbol UBER Website https://www.uber.com\n\n## Financial Performance\n\nIn 2025, Uber Technologies's revenue was $52.02 billion, an increase of 18.28% compared to the previous year's $43.98 billion. Earnings were $10.05 billion, an increase of 2.00%.\n\n## Analyst Summary\n\nAccording to 50 analysts, the average rating for UBER stock is \"Buy.\" The 12-month stock price target is $100.86, which is an increase of 51.21% from the latest price.\n\nUber and Chinese autonomous vehicle maker Pony.ai plan to launch a robotaxi service in London as part of an expanded partnership to bring driverless cars to Europe. The two companies said on Thursday ...\n\n16 days ago - TechCrunch\n\n### Sur la table to join Uber Eats marketplace\n\nUber (UBER) Technologies and Sur la table announced that Sur la table is joining the Uber Eats marketplace, making its curated assortment of kitchenware available for on-demand or scheduled delivery.\n\n### Sur la table Arrives on Uber Eats, Delivering Chef-Trusted Kitchen Gear to Customers Nationwide\n\n### Uber Eats Enters Catering Space With $2.3 Billion ezCater Deal\n\n### Uber delivery workers will pick up bigger restaurant orders as it enters catering\n\n### Uber to Acquire ezCater for $2.3 Billion in Food-Delivery Expansion\n\nUber expects the catering platform, with average orders exceeding $400, to boost its profit margins.\n\n### Uber is spending $2.3B to get into catering\n\nUber is buying a catering company called ezCater, as it continues to grow the types of services available through its Uber Eats division. It's an all-cash transaction valued at $2.3 billion.\n\n### M&A News: Uber Strikes $2.3B Deal for Baseball and Office Caterer ezCater","title":"Uber Technologies (UBER) Stock Price & Overview","url":"https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/uber/"},{"author":null,"id":"https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/uber/statistics/","image":"https://stockanalysis.com/stockanalysis-1200x630.png","text":"Uber Technologies (UBER) Statistics & Valuation\n\n66.70 -2.37 (-3.43%) At close: Oct 23, 2026, 4:00 PM EDT\n\n67.10 +0.40 (0.60%) After-hours: Oct 23, 2026, 7:59 PM EDT\n\n## Total Valuation\n\nUBER has a market cap or net worth of $136.24 billion. The enterprise value is $140.98 billion.\n\n| Market Cap | 136.24B |\n| --- | --- |\n| Enterprise Value | 140.98B |\n\n## Important Dates\n\nThe next confirmed earnings date is Wednesday, November 4, 2026, before market open.\n\n| Earnings Date | Nov 4, 2026 |\n| --- | --- |\n| Ex-Dividend Date | n/a |\n\n## Share Statistics\n\nUBER has 2.04 billion shares outstanding. The number of shares has decreased by -2.28% in one year.\n\n| Current Share Class | 2.04B |\n| --- | --- |\n| Shares Outstanding | 2.04B |\n| Shares Change (YoY) | -2.28% |\n| Shares Change (QoQ) | -1.02% |\n| Owned by Insiders (%) | 0.19% |\n| Owned by Institutions (%) | 83.61% |\n| Float | 2.04B |\n\n## Valuation Ratios\n\nThe trailing PE ratio is 14.55 and the forward PE ratio is 16.52. UBER's PEG ratio is 0.61.\n\n| PE Ratio | 14.55 |\n| --- | --- |\n| Forward PE | 16.52 |\n| PS Ratio | 2.47 |\n| Forward PS | 2.19 |\n| PB Ratio | 4.98 |\n| P/TBV Ratio | 8.15 |\n| P/FCF Ratio | 13.47 |\n| P/OCF Ratio | 13.07 |\n| PEG Ratio | 0.61 |\n\n## Enterprise Valuation\n\nThe stock's EV/EBITDA ratio is 18.86, with an EV/FCF ratio of 13.94.\n\n| EV / Earnings | 14.72 |\