people to connect and share with friends and family through mobile devices, personal computers, virtual reality (VR) headsets, and AI glasses in the United States, Canada, Europe, Asia-Pacific, and internationally. It operates through two segments, Family of Apps (FoA) and Reality Labs (RL). The FoA segment offers Facebook, which enables people to build community through feed, reels, stories, groups, marketplace, and other; Instagram that brings people closer through Instag... [Read more]\n\nIndustry Internet Content & Information\n\nSector Communication Services\n\nIPO Date May 18, 2012\n\nEmployees 75,472\n\nStock Exchange Nasdaq\n\nTicker Symbol META\n\nWebsite https://www.meta.com\n\n## Financial Performance\n\nIn 2025, Meta Platforms's revenue was $200.97 billion, an increase of 22.17% compared to the previous year's $164.50 billion. Earnings were $60.46 billion, a decrease of -3.05%.\n\n## Analyst Summary\n\nAccording to 62 analysts, the average rating for META stock is \"Strong Buy.\" The 12-month stock price target is $843.39, which is an increase of 31.24% from the latest price.\n\nPrice Target $843.39 (31.24% upside) Analyst Consensus: Strong Buy\n\n### Opinion | New Mexico Tries to Censor Meta\n\nA judge and the state AG say Facebook didn't block enough political speech.\n\n2 days ago - WSJ\n\n### Meta's massive deal for Zuckerberg proves execs aren't exempt from IRL work\n\nMeta is offering CEO Mark Zuckerberg a $20 billion stock deal to keep him close to its headquarters. The move speaks to a common belief that the best work happens when everyone is together in person.\n\n2 days ago - Business Insider\n\n### Soros-backed New Mexico AG behind $25B Meta lawsuit accused of seeking ‘tax on speech'\n\nNew Mexico Attorney General Raúl Torrez entered into politics with a 2016 run for district attorney backed by more than $100,000 in spending from a George Soros-funded super PAC.\n\n2 days ago - New York Post\n\n### Mark Zuckerberg Plots Deal to Pay Wealth Tax,